<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chameria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chameria is a coastal region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the far south of Albania, lying roughly between the Kalamas river and Butrint. Albanian clans settled there in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and it formed part of the Despotate of Epirus and later of Ottoman Epirus. Its Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> Albanian population was expelled into Albania in 1944–1945, an event still disputed between the two countries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chameria.jpg" alt="Chameria" width="320" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexikoua · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsamouria.Chameria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
